enericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"G","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P","text":"DirectedGraph","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"It keeps a copy of the graph to look vertices up through the graph’s own vertex indices, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"component(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" hashes nothing on a graph whose indices are its vertices. The copy shares","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"storage (copy-on-write), so making it is O(1), and later changes to the original do not affect","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the result. The cost comes later: while the result is alive, the next mutation of the original","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"copies the whole graph, as it would with any other copy. Drop the result, or keep only what","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"you need from it (","type":"text"},{"code":"Array(components)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), before mutating the graph.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A component’s slice keeps the indices of the flat storage it is cut from, as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"CompressedSparseRow.successors(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" does: use ","type":"text"},{"code":"first","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", iteration or ","type":"text"},{"code":"Array(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", not ","type":"text"},{"code":"[0]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Because its type names the graph’s type, a result cannot be returned through an existen